// Pulling an overlong block into a helper function (E0201). One block per
// function per round, outermost first, and only in a function that no other
// repair touched in this round: both would edit the same text. The helper is a
// new file next to the function's own; the locals the block reads become its
// parameters, and the one local it assigns that is read after it is its
// result. A block that cannot be pulled out soundly is reported with the
// reason (fix_xwhy) and left alone, and the next overlong block is tried.

fix_extract(int xef, int xelo) {
  int xtry = 0;
  fix_xattempt(xef, xelo, xtry);
  while((import fixx_again)[0] == 1 && xtry < len((import nst))) {
    xtry = xtry + 1;
    fix_xattempt(xef, xelo, xtry);
  }
} return void;
given fix_xplanned (7, 0):() then calls fix_xplan:(7, 0)
given fix_xplanned (10, 0):() then calls fix_xattempt:(10, 0, 0)
given fix_xplanned (10, 0):() then calls fix_xplan:[0]
given fix_xplanned (7, 0):() then calls fix_xattempt:[1]

fix_xplan(int xpf, int xplo) {
  int xpa = (import nst)[(import fixx_hit)[0]];
  int xpb = fix_xend();
  fix_xscan(xpf, xpa, xpb);
} chain (int xpf, int xplo) {
  string xpwhy = fix_xwhy(xpa, xpb);
  fix_xjudge(xpf, xplo, xpa, xpb, xpwhy);
} return void;
